.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116415","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116415.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116415.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR adds a Trail2D Node to Godot.\r\nThis would close https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6145\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f43b39f-93f4-4772-9f49-8ff33ccca564\r\n\r\n<img width=\"427\" height=\"1123\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a0ad56c-991a-4748-bb63-31e229a348de\" />\r\n\r\nIt is currently in Draft as I'd like some feedback from artists regarding the use and settings and from other contributers regarding the technical implementation.\r\n\r\n**Artist Feedback:**\r\n- Are these settings enough to cover your use case?\r\n- What kind of APIs would you expect to be available for this? Would you expect to be able to alter the trail through scripting, to for example add gravity or noise, or would it make more sense to add \"time\" data to the mesh data to access it through a shader for those kind of effects?\r\n\r\nImplementation Feedback\r\n- Is this implementation performant enough? It is fully done on the CPU using the LineBuilder helper class from Line2D.\r\n- Is it ok that I point to the Line2D enums for stuff like `Line2D::LineTextureMode` and `Line2D::LineJointMode` or should they be moved to a common class or copied over?\r\n- Would it make more sense to make a new common class that both Line2D and Trail2D inherit from and move shared stuff in there?","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116415/reactions","total_count":88,"+1":47,"-1":0,"laugh":6,"hooray":11,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":13,"eyes":7},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116415/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}